---
/**
 * About (docs/SPEC.md, Pages without designs): origin story (warm), approach,
 * people, and governance (plain). Unconfirmed content stays as placeholders.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { getSettings } from '../lib/content';

const settings = await getSettings();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={`Who Dandelion Club is, how we work, and how ${settings.npcName} governs it.`}
>
  <PageIntro eyebrow="About" title="About Dandelion Club.">
    We believe productive landscapes can change more than landscapes.
  </PageIntro>

  <Section ground="paper" width="text" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
    <SectionHeading eyebrow="How it started" id="story-heading">
      Our story.
    </SectionHeading>
    <div class="t-body stack">
      <p>Dandelion Club began with a simple observation.</p>
      <p>
        Across our communities there are pieces of land with enormous potential: school grounds,
        community spaces, forgotten corners and degraded soil.
      </p>
      <p>
        At the same time, many of the communities surrounding those spaces face increasing pressure
        from food insecurity, unemployment, environmental degradation and water scarcity.
      </p>
      <p>
        We don't see these as separate problems. We see a system. And systems can be redesigned.
      </p>
      <h3 class="sub">Why food forests?</h3>
      <p>
        Because a forest doesn't depend on one thing. Its resilience comes from diversity and
        relationship.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tall trees create shelter. Smaller plants occupy different layers. Roots work at different
        depths. Fallen material becomes food for the soil. Water is captured and cycled. Plants,
        fungi, insects, birds and microorganisms perform different jobs while supporting the whole.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our food forests are therefore not simply places where we plant fruit trees. They are places
        where we can explore how food production, ecological restoration, education, circular
        economy thinking, community participation and local enterprise can reinforce one another.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section ground="paper-sunk" aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
    <SectionHeading eyebrow="How we work" id="approach-heading">
      Our approach.
    </SectionHeading>
    <div class="t-body stack approach">
      <p>
        We don't arrive with a formula. We observe first. We listen to the people who know the
        place. We map the system. We look for resources that already exist. Then we design with
        nature rather than against it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sometimes that means trees. Sometimes it means compost. Sometimes it means capturing
        rainwater, propagating seedlings, solving a waste problem, creating a learning programme or
        connecting people who should know one another. Usually, it means several of those things at
        once.
      </p>
      <h3 class="sub">The long view</h3>
      <p>
        A tree planted today may take years to reach its full yield. That changes how you think
        about impact. Some results are immediate: people gathering, children learning, soil being
        covered, waste being diverted. Others take seasons. And some take years. We are interested
        in all three.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our goal is not simply to complete projects. It is to help establish living systems that
        communities can continue tending, adapting and benefiting from long after planting day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section ground="paper" aria-labelledby="people-heading">
    <SectionHeading eyebrow="Who we are" id="people-heading">
      The people.
    </SectionHeading>
    <p class="t-body people">
      <Placeholder value="TODO: people, each with a portrait (with consent), name and one line" />
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section ground="night" aria-labelledby="governance-heading">
    <div class="governance">
      <SectionHeading eyebrow="Governance" id="governance-heading">
        Accountable.
      </SectionHeading>
      <dl class="facts">
        <div class="fact">
          <dt class="t-eyebrow-sm">Run by</dt>
          <dd class="t-lead">{settings.npcName}</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <dt class="t-eyebrow-sm">NPC registration</dt>
          <dd class="t-detail">
            <Placeholder value={settings.npcRegistration} />
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <dt class="t-eyebrow-sm">Board</dt>
          <dd class="t-lead">
            <Placeholder value="TODO: board members and roles" />
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <dt class="t-eyebrow-sm">Section 18A</dt>
          <dd class="t-lead">
            {settings.section18a === true ? (
              'We can issue Section 18A tax certificates.'
            ) : settings.section18a === false ? (
              "We can't issue Section 18A tax certificates yet."
            ) : (
              <Placeholder value={settings.section18a} />
            )}
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <dt class="t-eyebrow-sm">Annual reports</dt>
          <dd class="t-lead">
            <Placeholder value="TODO: annual reports, once published" />
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
          <dt class="t-eyebrow-sm">Contact</dt>
          <dd class="t-lead">
            <a href={`mailto:${settings.email}`}>{settings.email}</a>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <div class="governance__actions">
        <Button href="/get-involved/partner">Partner with us</Button>
        <Button href="/donate" variant="ghost">
          Donate
        </Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .stack,
  .people {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }

  .stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    max-width: var(--measure-text);
  }

  .sub {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--type-subtitle-size);
    line-height: var(--type-subtitle-leading);
    font-weight: var(--type-subtitle-weight);
  }

  .governance {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .fact {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--hairline-on-night);
  }

  .fact dt {
    color: var(--dandelion);
  }

  .fact a {
    color: var(--dandelion);
  }

  .governance__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .facts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .facts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
